## 5. Accessibility Baseline

[Normative requirements. Every L2 spec inheriting from this L1 must comply with everything in this section.]

- **WCAG version and level:** [e.g., WCAG 2.2 Level AA]
- **Minimum contrast — text:** [e.g., 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text]
- **Minimum contrast — UI components:** [e.g., 3:1 for interactive elements against adjacent colors]
- **Keyboard navigation:** [e.g., All interactive elements must be reachable and operable by keyboard alone]
- **Focus indicators:** [Visible focus ring using color-focus-ring + shadow-focus on all interactive elements]
- **Touch targets:** [e.g., Minimum 44×44px for all tappable elements]
- **Motion safety:** [All animations must be disabled when prefers-reduced-motion is set]
- **Screen reader:** [ARIA roles and labels required on all interactive elements; test with NVDA/JAWS on Windows, VoiceOver on macOS/iOS]
- **Color meaning:** [Color must never be the sole differentiator for information]

---

## 6. AI Generation Rules

### Generate

[What AI agents are authorized to produce from specs that inherit this L1:]
- [e.g., Component markup in HTML/CSS/React using system tokens]
- [e.g., State variants as defined in L2 specs]
- [e.g., Accessibility attributes consistent with section 5 requirements]

### Validate

[What agents must verify in output before considering it compliant:]
- [ ] All color values reference named system tokens — no hex, RGB, or HSL literals
- [ ] All spacing values reference named spacing tokens
- [ ] Typography uses named typography tokens only
- [ ] All interactive elements include keyboard accessibility attributes
- [ ] Contrast ratios meet section 5 minimums
- [ ] No element uses a color token outside its defined intent

### Forbidden

[What agents must never generate regardless of instruction:]
- Raw color values not defined in the Token Contract
- Components or patterns not defined in an ACTIVE L2 spec
- WCAG 2.2 AA-non-compliant output
- [Add system-specific forbidden items]

### Prompt Seed

```
You are generating UI for [System Name], governed by SDDn Foundation Spec [SYSTEM-L1-NNN] v[version].

Before generating any output:
1. Confirm all color, spacing, typography, radius, shadow, and motion values map to named tokens in the Token Contract.
2. Confirm all interactive elements meet the Accessibility Baseline (WCAG 2.2 AA, keyboard navigable, 44px touch targets).
3. Check that the component or pattern has an ACTIVE L2 spec. If not, halt and ask.

Do not generate: [key forbidden items for this system]
```

